Author: Paul Nicholson <271459+pwnicholson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Apr 11 14:52:28 2026 -0500

    v1.6.0 - Palette editor overhaul, texture pack import, editor palette render option
    
    - New PALETTE: 1111 entries from Java texture averages (palette.json)
    - Palette Editor: texture pack import (zip/mcpack/folder) with threaded
      extraction, indeterminate progress dialog, and cancel support
    - Palette Editor: conflict resolution dialog for same-block different-color merges
    - Palette Editor: texture pack preview dialog with filter + select/deselect all
    - Palette Editor: open palette prompts Add/Replace when palette already loaded
    - Palette Editor: _pal_merge_dict / _pal_load_merge / _pal_from_texture_pack
    - Palette Editor: transparent checkbox now preserves list scroll position
    - Render options: 'Use palette loaded in palette editor' checkbox (timelapse
      and single-map tabs) - editor palette checked first, falls back to default
      palette, unknown blocks still logged to unknown_blocks.json
    - RenderOptions: use_editor_palette + editor_palette fields; palette snapshotted
      at render start so mid-render editor changes don't affect the running job
    - classify_block: accepts optional extra_palette kwarg
    - Help tab: full Palette Editor section covering lookup priority, workflow,
      texture pack import, merge/conflict, transparent blocks, and save procedure

